<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28201" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοῦπος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>any dead, heavy sound, thud,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἀκόντων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.364
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				16.361
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ὀρώρει πύργων βαλλομένων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					9.573
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				12.289
			</span></i>; of the distant <i>din</i> of battle, <i><span class="en">
				16.635
			</span></i>; of the <i>sound</i> of footsteps, <i><span class="en">
				10.354
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				16.10
			</span></i>; of <i>the measured tread</i> of infantry, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				23.234
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				70
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅμαδον καὶ δ.,</span> of a
			multitude, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				10.556
			</span></i>; of the <i>roar</i> of the sea dashing against rocks or of
			a distant torrent, <i><span class="en">
				5.401
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.455
			</span></i>.—Rare in Trag., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. μαράγνης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					376
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χερόπλακτοι δ᾽ ἐν στέρνοισι
				πεσοῦνται δοῦποι</span> the <i>loud</i> beating of
			breasts, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				634
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				513
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκούομεν πυλῶν δ.</span>
			<i>the noise</i> of opening gates, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ion</u>
				516
			</span></i>. Rare in Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.22
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψόφον</span>
			)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; θόρυβος καὶ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					2.2.19
				</span></i>
			.</div>
